title: Don't let breaking a dead lock delete a live one
created: 2026-10-24T10:26:39Z
updated: 2026-10-24T10:26:39Z
effort: M
area: cli
handoff:

Ported from IDOL's vendored copy (IDOL 1368), where it was found and fixed.

lock() broke a lock whose owner was dead with a bare rm -f .lock. Two
contenders can both read the dead owner X; if the first breaks the lock
and publishes its own before the second reaches its rm, that rm deletes
the first one's live lock and both walk in: two writers on one ticket.

Fix: break X's lock only while holding .lock.X.brk (published with
link(2) like the lock), re-reading .lock under it and removing it only if
it still names X. A .brk held by a live process is waited on like a live
lock; a dead breaker's .brk with the lock gone is litter and is cleared;
a dead breaker with X's lock still there stops and names both files to
remove by hand. The generated reference says so.

Done when claim.sh drives the race with parked rm/ln wrappers and pins
the wedge and litter cases.
